πνεῦμα, -τος, τό, 
[in LXX chiefly and very frequently for רוּחַ ;] 
__1. of air in motion; 
__(a) wind: Jhn.3.8 pl., Heb.1.7 (LXX); 
__(b) breath: π. ζωῆς, Rev.11.11 π. τοῦ στόματος, figuratively, 2Th.2.8 (cf. Ps 32 (33)6). 
__2. Of the vital principle, the spirit (Arist., Polyb., al.): Luk.8.55, Jhn.19.30, Act.7.59, al.; opposite to σάρξ, Mat.26.41, Mrk.14.38, 1Co.5.5, al.; to σῶμα, Rom.8.10, 1Co.6.17; 7.34,…

